  "summary": "In 2 Samuel 5:7–9, Zion names the stronghold David captures, which the narrative then calls the city of David. This places Zion within Jerusalem's royal story. The record's later temple passages concern worship in Jerusalem, but they do not map every biblical use or boundary of the name Zion.",
  "historical_context": "Second Samuel 5:1–10 narrates David's capture of Jerusalem and its stronghold, Zion, then describes his residence and building activity in the city. The passage connects Zion with the city of David in this episode; it does not establish the exact boundaries of the name in every later text or provide an archaeological reconstruction.",
